<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Gabriel Stedman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1744">1744</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Gabriel Stedman was a Scottish-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> soldier who served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> from 1773 to 1777 with Dutch troops sent to fight the maroons led by Boni. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narrative-of-a-five-years-expedition">Narrative of a Five Years Expedition against the Revolted Negroes of Surinam</a>, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1796 with engravings by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-blake">William Blake</a> among others, described plantation <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> and its cruelties in vivid detail and became an important text in the debate over abolition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-gabriel-stedman.jpg" alt="John Gabriel Stedman" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Gabriel Stedman / Francesco Bartolozzi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bartolozzi_-_John_Gabriel_Stedman_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When new maroon groups led by Boni attacked plantations in the 1770s, the colony called in Dutch troops, among them the soldier <b>John Gabriel Stedman</b>, formed a corps of Black Rangers from slaves freed for the purpose and built a defensive cordon path around the plantation zone.</blockquote><a href="/empire/suriname">Suriname · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Dendermonde, in what is now <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>. Died in Tiverton, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.03,4.1&amp;year=1778" aria-label="Dendermonde on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4643 394 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of John Gabriel Stedman"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5093 664h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5093 664h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.03,4.1&amp;year=1778">What was here in 1778? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
